    <string name="about_tagline">An open catalog of open-source Android apps</string>
    <string name="about_description">OpenAndroid Store installs and updates apps listed in a public catalog. Every app in it has open source code.</string>
    <string name="about_rules_title">How apps get here</string>
    <string name="about_rules">• Developers add an app by opening a pull request in the catalog repository
• Only apps with public source code and an open license are accepted
• Each pull request is checked by hand before it is merged
• The catalog stores a checksum and the signing key of every release</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_title">Privacy and safety</string>
    <string name="about_privacy">The store has no accounts, ads or analytics. It talks only to the catalog address and to GitHub when downloading. Before installing, it checks the file checksum, the package name and the signing key. Updates are accepted only with the same signing key.</string>
